+# Full study — S5-CLM-00003495
+
+## Mathematical statement
+
+For the frozen function `F = maximalLength`, if some `n > 1` satisfies
+`F n = n^e`, then eventually `m^e ≤ F m` along the natural-number filter at
+infinity.  The provider snapshot marks this theorem FC-SORRY: its source body
+is not proof authority.
+
+## Semantic identity
+
+The exact provider module, qualified declaration, source bytes, declaration
+bytes, type digest, revision, and transitive non-foundation census are pinned
+in `statement-crosswalk.json`.  No local definition or notation reinterprets a
+source symbol.  The target proposition preserves both hypotheses and the
+eventual-order output.
+
+## Proof/composition study
+
+The proof-unit graph has a single conclusion node, two hypothesis nodes, and a
+semantic-transport node.  Edges are typed and reverse-readable.  The provider
+`sorryAx` is a trust boundary, not a proof edge.  Master replay must establish
+the exact root independently.
+
+## Readability and release
+
+Every required node maps injectively to an anchored fragment and every anchor
+maps back to one node.  Prose is distilled into structured inventories without
+deleting mathematical content.  The release record is provisional until the
+canonical Master verifies M0, R0, current trace, mutation replay, and strict
+dominance over THM-M-0387.
